history of our country. Biden had like 9%-10% inflation, and I inherited that, and we have it way down.\n  + Claimed without providing evidence, quoted in \"Trump says Iran agrees to ‘no nuclear,’ and other takeaways from new interview\" Washington Examiner (June 3, 2026)\n\n* It'll last for 50 to 100 years before you have to do anything with it.\n  + Claimed about the results of renovation of the Lincoln Memorial reflecting pool, quoted in \"After D.C.'s Reflecting Pool gets repainted, visitors ask: What changed?\" NPR (June 5, 2026)\n\n* I love the inflation.\n\n* The United States will be hitting Iran (Whose Navy, Air Force, Radar, Anti Aircraft, and all other forms of Defense, together with most of its offensive capability, are GONE!), VERY HARD TONIGHT. At some point in the not too distant future, we will be taking Kharg Island, and other oil infrastructure points, and assume total control of their Oil and Gas Markets.\n  + \"Trump says US will ‘be taking’ Kharg Island in latest Iran war threat\" Al Jazeera (June 11, 2026)\n\n* I don’t know if you heard, but we ended the war with Iran today. They have agreed never to have a nuclear weapon, something that we insisted on; that was the whole purpose. That was 95 percent of it.\n  + \"We ended the war with Iran today,\" Trump says CNN (June 12, 2026)\n\n* Qatar is the closest to Iran, physically. With other countries, I noticed they had to travel about 45 minutes to get there. With you, you could walk right across the border.\n  + \"Donald Trump Doesn’t Know Anything About Geography\" The New Republic / Yahoo News (June 16, 2026)\n\n* So happy for highly respected Congressman Mike Collins. He will win his Senate Race in Georgia against a pathetic failed Dumocrat Senator, Os(jerk!)off, who is a joke in D.C. Nobody even knows who he is!!! I'll be doing Big TRUMP Rallies for Mike in Georgia! President DJT.\n  + Social media post, quoted in \"Trump Drops Childish New Nickname For Democratic Star\" Yahoo News / Huffington Post (June 17, 2026)\n\n* If it works out, I'm going to take the credit. If it doesn't work out, I'm blaming JD.\n  + Claimed about a memorandum of understanding about engaging in negotiations about restoring peace after the US attack on Iran, quoted in \"Trump finally said it out loud: JD Vance is his Iran fall guy\" AOL (June 17, 2026)\n\n* POLL: Which do you prefer, Dumocrat or Dumbocrat? In one case, you simply exchange the ‘e’ for ‘u,’ so simple and precise (Many people don’t know, or assume, that DUMB ends in ‘b’). In the other case, you spell out DUMB, but it seems to lose some of the identity to Democrats when done this way. Which is better?\n  + \"D-U-M-B: Trump gives spelling lesson as he works on nicknames for his rivals\" Independent (June 20, 2026)\n\n#### July 2026\n\n* American Liberty has not endured for 250 years merely because of words on paper. Liberty has prevailed here because of the culture and character of the people who declared it, defended it, and preserved it. . . . In recent years, there has been an undeniable attempt to change this exceptional Character, to beat the American Spirit out of us, alienate us from our history, and make it impossible to even answer the question \"What does it mean to be an American?\"\n  + Address at the Mount Rushmore National Memorial in Keystone, SD (July 3, 2026); \"Travel Pool Report No. 8 — speech start and excerpts\", White House Press Pool\n\n* RESTRAINING ORDER NEEDED\n  + Written on social media about Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, quoted in \"Jilted Trump, 80, Taunts Female World Leader With Creepy Meme\" The Daily Beast (July 6, 2026)\n\n* Spain is a terrible partner in NATO. They don’t participate. They don’t pay. I don’t want anything to do with Spain. Cut off all trade with Spain, please, including visits. Don’t even talk to them. They’re hopeless, bad people.\n  + \"Trump says he doesn’t want anything to do with Spain: ‘Cut off all trade’\" CNBC (July 9, 2026)\n\n* We had 111 missiles shot by the Islamic Republic of Japan\n  + Said at the 2026 Ankara NATO summit, quoted in \"Trump confuses Iran for US ally in Zelensky Q&A: ‘We had 111 missiles shot by the Islamic Republic of Japan’ The Independent (July 9th, 2026)\n\n* We are holding Canada responsible for the fact that they are not properly maintaining their Forests, and Brush therein, and the United States is being unnecessarily invaded by filthy, polluted, and unhealthy air, the quality of which is dangerous, and totally unacceptable!”\n* I will call the Prime Minister during the day to find out what they are going to do about it. The cost is incalculable! Canada has refused to engage in basic Forest Management and Debris Removal, knowing that such refusal will lead to exactly this result. This is Willful Negligence, and becoming a yearly occurrence, costing the United States Billions of Dollars, which cost of this pollution must of necessity be added to the TARIFFS Canada is currently paying.\n  + \"Trump threatens Canada over wildfire smoke choking U.S. cities\" Politico (July 17, 2026)\n* On incoming British Prime Minister, Andy Burnham: \"I don’t know, I think I see that he was, I guess, the mayor of a town. I hear he’s extremely liberal, extremely, so that means he probably won’t open up the North Sea.\"\n  + \"‘I hear he’s extremely liberal’: Trump offers first comments on Andy Burnham\" The Guardian (June 28, 2026)\n\n* I only like people who like me.\n  + \"Trump on Jordan vs. LeBron debate: 'I only like people who like me'\" Fox News (July 24, 2026)\n\n* THE MAN WHO SAVED AMERICA\n  + Written on a collage of pictures of Trump, in one of more than 100 social media postings from Trump during the night between July 26 and 27, 2026, quoted in \"Trump floods social media with AI images targeting rivals and promoting 'Trump 2028'\" CNBC TV 18 (July 27, 20218)\n\n#### August 2026\n\n* About US voters:\n\n* A lot of them are very angry at Republicans, to be honest with you ... they are not angry with me, but they are angry with Republicans.\n  + \"GREATEST PRESIDENT\" Daily Mail (August 9, 2026)\n\n* A lot of people are saying I’m one of the greatest presidents ever.\n  + \"GREATEST PRESIDENT\" Daily Mail (August 9, 2026)\n\n* Pretty soon, I will be declaring the Hormuz Strait a territory of the United States,\n  + \"Iran rejects Trump’s ‘delusions’ on making Strait of Hormuz a US territory\" The Hill (August 15, 2026)\n\n* Canada wants the benefits of being a State, without being one!!! They have also charged our great farmers, for many years, massive amounts of Tariffs. No more!!!”\n  + \"Trump accuses Canada of wanting ‘benefits of being a State, without being one’ amid trade war\" The Hill (August 23, 2026)\n\n* The United States is giving serious consideration to changing the name of Lake Ontario to Lake America in that we don’t expect to doing much business with Ontario any longer.\n  + \"Trump floats renaming Lake Ontario to ‘Lake America’ as feud with Canada escalates\" CNN (August 25, 2026)\n\n* About Dolly Parton:\n\n* She really liked me.\n  + \"Trump Claims Dolly Parton ‘Really Liked Me,' She Just Didn't Want Anyone To Know\" Huffington Post / Yahoo News (August 26, 2026)\n\n* Affordability is interesting because the Democrats caused affordability.\n* I inherited high prices, and then from the first day, they started using the word ‘affordability'. It was a new word. Nobody ever heard the word.\n  + \"Republicans are dismissing affordability. That could be a problem in November\" CNBC (August 26, 2026)\n\n* About the Strait of Hormuz\n\n* The mines are gone. You probably saw that – we put it out yesterday – all the mines, we got rid of the mines\n  + \"US allies warn Hormuz Strait is still mined despite Trump claim\" Strait Times (August 27, 2026)\n\n#### September 2026\n\n* We like getting along with everybody. One of the reasons that I'm so successful, I get along with everybody.\n  + \"Trump Defends Hosting Russia at G20 as Europeans Voice Disapproval\" Time Magazine (September 1, 2026)\n\n* We could do tremendous good for ourselves by just not trading with other countries.\n* If I don't trade with Mexico, they have nothing that we have to have. I mean, hot tamales? Tomatoes? A couple of things? Basically, they have nothing we need. We have oil. We have everything.\n* We lose with the European Union $200 billion a year. If I did not trade with them, we would lose nothing. Just one swipe of the pen.\n* We would save from $60 billion a year to $90 billion a year just by not trading with Canada.\n* In Norway, they don't like me because I think they think I'm a little conservative.\n  + \"Trump: 'We Could Do Tremendous Good For Ourselves By Just Not Trading With Other Countries'\" Politico / Yahoo (September 4, 2026)\n* To the victor belong the spoils.\n  + “Trump Tells Leaders He Will Reach a Deal With Iran or ‘Annihilate’ It” (print, jump, headline), at the United Nations, The New York Times (23 Sept 2026), in regards to Venezuela.\n* I have a big decision to make, will a deal be made with Iran that lets them rebuild and create a far greater country than it ever was before - maybe one of the greatest in the Middle East or even the world? Or do I annihilate the Islamic Republic and do it quickly, never giving them a chance to kill and destroy people and countries again?\n  + “Trump Tells U.N. Iran Faces A Risk Of Obliteration” (print headline), The New York Times (23 Sept 2026), front page.\n\n#### October 2026\n\n* About the U.S. attack on Iran:\n\n* It’s a small price to pay for keeping the world safe, keeping our country safe. They can take out a city, let ’em take out Los Angeles, let ’em take out San Diego. This is a very small price to pay.\n  + \"Trump suggests letting Iran ‘take out’ Los Angeles and San Diego at campaign rally\" Los Angeles Times (October 5, 2026)\n\n* All your prices have been tumbling down. In fact, oil is less than it was under Biden.\n  + Claimed without providing evidence, quoted in \"'We Are Saving The World': Trump Says Iran War Will End Soon, Prices Will Come Down\" NDTV Profit (October 6, 2026)\n\n* I could say the stupidest things and you'd clap.\n* If Republicans get in power, you're going to end up in a depression. These people are incompetent.\n  + \"Trump Tells Supporters: ‘I Could Say The Stupidest Things And You’d Clap’\" Forbes / Yahoo News (October 11, 2026)\n\n* Effective immediately, there is an ENERGY CEASEFIRE in the War between Russian and Ukraine. Both parties have agreed.\n  + Claimed without providing evidence, quoted in \"Trump claims ‘energy ceasefire,’ but Ukraine says Russia keeps striking its energy facilities\" NBC News (October 12, 2026)\n\n* Russia, frankly, has been fine on Ukraine. They haven't been doing much.\n  + \"What Russia's doing to Ukraine is 'fine,' Trump says\" Kyiv Independent (October 19, 2026)\n\n* I didn't get the Nobel Prize. I didn't get the Pulitzer. I should have gotten the Pulitzer for writing, too.\n  + \"Trump was in South Carolina to save midterm seat — then he moaned about not winning Nobel Prize\" Independent (October 22, 2026)\n\n* I don't ramble. I got ten — I know everything I'm so — I got aptitude that they dream about, so you know, they'll say he rambled. No, no, as long as the stories keep coming back. You know. As long as — no, but I just — I'm in a good mood today. Think of it. I won the presidency.\n  + \"Trump's Self-Awareness Plummets To Staggering Depths In Bonkers Boast\" Huffington Post / Yahoo News (October 22, 2026)\n\n* My uncle invented radar, can you believe it?\n  + \"Trump makes ‘ridiculous’ claim about his uncle – and is swiftly fact-checked\" Indy 100 (October 25, 2026)\n\n* They just call her Kamala. You know, if you ask somebody, let's do a test, how many people know her last name? Like about five. Kamala, you just call her Kamala. Kamala Harris -- it's funny, a simple name like Harris and nobody has -- a complicated name like Kamala. It's Kamela, Kumala, Kamala, Kumala -- nobody knows how to pronounce it yet, I don't know.\n  + \"Speech: Donald Trump Holds a Midterm Political Rally in Corpus Christi, Texas - October 27, 2026\" Rollcall factbase (October 27, 2026)\n\n* You need about 190 IQ to figure out the ballot. They put a ballot down where they're talking about 'incumbent' Republican, and the other one. Most people don't know in Alaska — and a lot of other states, too — what does incumbent mean? I don't know what incumbent means. Incumbent!\n  + \"Trump Again Insults Alaska Republicans Over Belief Most Don’t Know What ‘Incumbent’ Means\" The Wrap / Yahoo (October 30, 2026)\n\n* I wasn't on the Ballot and if I was, we would have won IN A LANDSLIDE!\n  + \"'I wasn't on the ballot': Trump distances himself from midterm results\" USA Today (November 4, 2026)\n\n## Disputed\n\n* We have certain things in common, Jeffrey.\n* Enigmas never age, have you noticed that?\n* A pal is a wonderful thing. Happy Birthday – and may every day be another wonderful secret.\n  + Written in a letter to Jeffrey Epstein, according to \"Jeffrey Epstein’s Friends Sent Him Bawdy Letters for a 50th Birthday Album. One Was From Donald Trump.\" Wall Street Journal (Article behind pay wall) (July 17, 2025). Quoted in \"Trump requests release of Epstein grand jury transcripts amid report of ‘bawdy’ birthday note\" The Guardian (July 18, 2025). Disputed by Donald Trump.\n\n* These people should be executed. They are scumbags.\n  + About whistleblowers and journalists. Attributed by John Bolton in The Room Where It Happened, Simon & Schuster, 2020, p. 290 . ISBN 978-1-9821-4805-8.\n\n* Do you still like having sex with your wife? How often? You must have had a better fuck than your wife? Tell me about it. I have girls coming in from Los Angeles at three o'clock. We can go upstairs and have a great time. I promise.\n  + Reported by Michael Wolff in Fire and Fury: Inside the Trump White House (5 January 2018)\n\n* I hope you can see your way clear to letting this go, to letting Flynn go. He is a good guy. I hope you can let this go.\n  + Reported as being the words of President Trump recorded in a memo that James Comey, FBI Director at the time, wrote shortly after a meeting held in the Oval Office on 14 February 2017, referring to the federal investigation into links to the Russian government of national security adviser, Michael T. Flynn, who had resigned the day before. In a statement, the White House has denied the version of events in the memo. — New York Times (16 May 2017)\n  + Comey confirmed under oath his account of Trump's words while appearing before the Senate Intelligence Committee (8 June 2017)\n  + When asked about Comey's testimony during a press conference on 9 June 2017, Trump said, \"I didn't say that. I will tell you I didn't say that. And there'd be nothing wrong if I did say it according to everybody that I've read today, but I did not say that.\"\n\n* Why are we having all these people from shithole countries come here?\n  + Reportedly said in a meeting with lawmakers on immigration, as quoted in \"Trump criticized immigration from 's---hole' countries: report\" (11 January 2018), by Avery Anapol, The Hill. Variant: \"Why do we want all these people from shithole countries coming here?\" As quoted in Trump's 'shithole' comment is his new rock bottom, CNN, 12 January 2018. Trump denied making this comment.\n    - \"The language used by me at the DACA meeting was tough, but this was not the language used.\" Tweet by @realDonaldTrump (12 January 2018)\n* Reportedly said in a meeting with lawmakers on immigration, as quoted in \"Trump criticized immigration from 's---hole' countries: report\" (11 January 2018), by Avery Anapol, The Hill. Variant: \"Why do we want all these people from shithole countries coming here?\" As quoted in Trump's 'shithole' comment is his new rock bottom, CNN, 12 January 2018. Trump denied making this comment.\n\n* Why do we want all these people from Africa here? They're shithole countries ... We should have more people from Norway.\n  + 12 January 2018, per Reuters' source\n  + In December 2025 Trump said: \"Remember I said that to the senators that came in, the Democrats. They wanted to be bipartisan. So they came in. And they said, ‘This is totally off the record, nothing mentioned here, we want to be honest,’ because our country was going to hell. And we had a meeting. And I say: Why is it we only take people from shithole countries, right? Why can’t we have some people from Norway, Sweden – just a few – let us have a few. From Denmark – do you mind sending us a few people? Send us some nice people, do you mind? But we always take people from Somalia. Places that are a disaster, right? Filthy, dirty, disgusting, ridden with crime.\n    - \"Almost eight years later, Trump confirms he used the phrase ‘shithole countries’\" CNN (December 10, 2025)\n\n* Why do we need more Haitians? Take them out.\n  + Reportedly said in a meeting with lawmakers on immigration, as quoted in \"'Sh\\*thole countries' respond to Trump's rhetoric\", CBS News. Trump denied making this comment.\n  + \"Never said anything derogatory about Haitians other than Haiti is, obviously, a very poor and troubled country. Never said \"take them out.\" Made up by Dems. I have a wonderful relationship with Haitians. Probably should record future meetings - unfortunately, no trust!\" Tweet by @realDonaldTrump (12 January 2018)\n\n* [B]lack people are too stupid to vote for me.\n  + As quoted in \"Michael Cohen Says Trump Repeatedly Used Racist Language in Private\" (2 November 2018), by Emily Jane Fox, Vanity Fair. In a post-2018 midterm press conference, Trump denied making the comment and dismissed Cohen's claims: \"That's false\" — as quoted in \"President Trump says he has 'never used racist remarks'\" (7 November 2018), by Hunter Walker, Yahoo News.\n\n* Name one country run by a black person that's not a shithole... Name one city.\n  + As quoted in \"Michael Cohen Says Trump Repeatedly Used Racist Language in Private\" (2 November 2018), by Emily Jane Fox, Vanity Fair. \"White House press secretary Sarah Huckabee Sanders denied those comments at the time.\"\n\n* Why should I go to that cemetery? It’s filled with losers .. suckers .. Who were the good guys in this war?\n  + Saturday 10 November 2018 two hours before a scheduled 30-minute helicopter ride from Paris to the Aisne-Marne American Cemetery, the visit was cancelled with White House stating a rainy forecast made it too dangerous\n  + 3 September 2020 TheAtlantic.com writer Jeffrey Goldberg stated that \"four people with firsthand knowledge of the discussion that day\" (Goldberg did not provide any names) that \"Trump rejected the idea of the visit because he feared his hair would become disheveled in the rain, and because he did not believe it important to honor American war dead\", and described the two-sentence quote above as part of \"a conversation with senior staff members on the morning of the scheduled visit\".\n    - Goldberg also stated that during the trip (in a separate conversation) that Trump used the term \"suckers\" to collectively describe the 1800+ marines who died at Belleau Wood, but did not provide any surrounding words (the purported quote was the only word in quotation marks)\n    - the sentence about \"good guys\" Goldberg says was stated towards aides (not senior staff members)\n      * Goldberg did state a number regarding witness count of the other two statements, only for the \"losers\" one\n  + 4 September 2020 Trump responded to Goldberg's piece \"It’s a total lie. It’s fake news\".\n  + Trump also tweeted that day: \"The Atlantic Magazine is dying, like most magazines, so they make up a fake story in order to gain some relevance. Story already refuted, but this is what we are up against.\"\n  + press secretary Kayleigh McEnany also on September 4th stated \"The story in the Atlantic has been categorically debunked by eyewitnesses and contemporaneous documents\", quoting two service members:\n    - \"\"I was with the president the morning after the scheduled visit. He was extremely disappointed that arrangements could not be made to get him to the site and that the trip had been cancelled. I have worked with the president for his entire administration .. I have never heard him utter a disparaging remark of any kind about our troops.\" - Derek Lyons\n    - \"there was a bad weather called in France and that the helicopters were unable to safely make the flight. Overall, the president's support and respect for our American troops past and present is unquestionable\" - Dan Walsh\n  + following Goldberg's piece that same day, James LaPorta wrote on AP \"A senior Defense Department official with firsthand knowledge of events and a senior U.S. Marine Corps officer who was told about Trump’s comments confirmed some of the remarks to The Associated Press, including the 2018 cemetery comments.\"\n\n## Misattributed\n\n* I have a really high IQ, Phil. I mean, c'mon. It's impossible for me to not be atheist.\n  + Attributed by photo meme to an appearance on The Phil Donahue Show in 1989. According to Snopes.com, there is no evidence he ever said this, nor that he even appeared on The Phil Donahue Show in 1989.\n\n* This has been the worst trade deal in the history of trade deals, maybe ever.\n\n* If I were to run, I'd run as a Republican. They're the dumbest group of voters in the country. They believe anything on Fox News. I could lie and they'd still eat it up. I bet my numbers would be terrific.\n  + There is no record of Trump ever saying this; sometimes \"People magazine, 1998\" is incorrectly given as the \"source\" of this quotation — snopes.com; truthorfiction.com\n\n* The harder I work, the luckier I get.\n  + Originated with Samuel Goldwyn as a paraphrase of a proverb from a collection by Coleman Cox, but similar proverbs have existed since the 16th century.\n\n* People are dying today that have never died before.\n  + According to Snopes.com, there is no record of Trump saying this.\n\n* The doctors said they've never seen a body kill the Coronavirus like my body. They tested my DNA and it wasn't DNA. It was USA.\n  + Reportedly said by Trump after he was hospitalized with COVID-19, following an outbreak of the disease in the White House; the quote actually originates from an image featuring a fabricated subtitle overlaid on a video released by the President while he was in Walter Reed National Military Medical Center.\n\n* My blood IS the vaccine!!!!!\n  + Originates from a fabricated screenshot of a tweet allegedly posted on October 5, 2020, the same day Trump was released from Walter Reed National Military Medical Center after his diagnosis of COVID-19. The fictitious quote likely refers to the donation of the blood plasma of COVID-19 survivors as a treatment method against catching the disease, a treatment of which Trump has been a vocal supporter. Trump has, however, suggested that he would consider donating his own plasma for this purpose.\n\n## Quotes about Trump\n\n## See also\n\n* Donald Trump on social media\n* Donald Trump Jr.\n* Impeachment of Donald Trump\n* List of presidents of the United States\n* First presidency of Donald Trump\n* Second presidency of Donald Trump\n* Racial views of Donald Trump\n* Russian interference in the 2016 United States elections\n* 2020 United States presidential election\n\n## External links\n\n* Official website\n* \"Trump's Lies\" by David Leonhardt and Stuart A. Thompson - a catalog of \"nearly every outright lie he has told publicly\" in his first five months in office, in The New York Times (23 June 2017)\n\n* ↑ We Need an Interpreter to Work Out Trump’s ‘Debanking’ Rant. The Daily Beast (2024-01-21). Retrieved on 2024-01-21.\n* ↑ Luciano, Michael (2024-01-18). Huh? Trump Declares, ‘They Wanna De-Bank You and We’re Going to De-Bank’. Mediaite. Retrieved on 2024-01-21.\n\n* Uncategorized article cleanup\n* Donald Trump\n* 1946 births\n* Living people\n* Businesspeople from New York City\n* Businesspeople in real estate\n* Conspiracy theorists\n* Politicians from Florida\n* Politicians from New York City\n* Presbyterians from the United States\n* Presidents of the United States\n* Memoirists from the United States\n* Nationalists\n* Non-fiction authors from the United States\n* People charged with crimes\n* Producers from the United States\n* Republican Party (United States) politicians\n* Television personalities\n* Television producers\n* United States presidential candidates, 2000\n* United States presidential candidates, 2016\n* United States presidential candidates, 2020\n* United States presidential candidates, 2024\n* University of Pennsylvania alumni\n* People associated with cryptocurrency\n* Time Person of the Year\n* Trump family","author":"Contributors to Wikimedia projects","published_date":"2004-04-18T07:27:17Z","latency_ms":7305.962855985854,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}